# promise: #717
# With the sidebar shown and a space to the right of the current one, opening the Library and closing it
# again (its button, ⇧⌘L) never shows the next space's tabs past the sidebar's edge: the column narrows from
# the Library's width to the tab list's, and the space pages' mask follows it at once (PagerMask, #679),
# where it used to ease after it and let the next space's column through for its 0.13 s.
budget rss=700 stalls50=10
cra://debug?windowSize=1280x800
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=first-space
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)
cra://action/newSpace
wait 1
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=second-space-a
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=second-space-b
wait 1
cra://action/space1
wait 1
cra://action/openLibrary
wait 1.5
cra://action/openLibrary
expect-log library left in place: the space pages' mask follows the column$
reject-log the space pages' mask trails the column
